.TH VIBECODER-SUPERVISOR 1 "2026-10-31" "vibecoder 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vibecoder-supervisor \- run and inspect the persistent vibecoder supervisor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibecoder-supervisor
.BI --config " FILE"
.RI { config-check | dry-run | status | jobs | once | run | reconcile | pause | resume }
.SH DESCRIPTION
Vibecoder coordinates approved Codex and GitHub workflows using persistent SQLite
state. The supervisor command provides continuous operation and diagnostics.
.PP
The Debian package starts with
.B operational_state=NOT_CONFIGURED
and will not select work until an administrator has validated the configuration and
changed it to
.BR READY .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vibecoder/supervisor.json
Supervisor configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/vibecoder/accounts.json
Non-secret account runtime references.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vibecoder
Persistent database, account homes and workspaces.
.SH OTHER COMMANDS
The package also installs vibecoder-agents, vibecoder-bootstrap, vibecoder-generate,
vibecoder-issues, vibecoder-live-setup, vibecoder-m00-diagnose, vibecoder-publish,
vibecoder-reviews, vibecoder-tasks and vibecoder-worker. Use
.B --help
on each command for its milestone-specific interface.
.SH SECURITY
Tokens are supplied externally and must not be stored in versioned configuration.
Vibecoder does not merge Pull Requests automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vibecoder-admin (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR git (1)
